+======================================================================================+
|                           ROD COIL — PHYSICS MODEL BLOCK                             |
|                     (Quartz Rod + Resistive Element — Abstract Only)                 |
+======================================================================================+

  PARAMETERS
  ----------
  R_COIL      = 1.8 Ω          ; nominal resistance
  ALPHA_T     = 0.0004 /°C     ; temp coefficient (conceptual)
  T_AMBIENT   = 25 °C          ; baseline temperature
  T_ROD       = variable       ; quartz rod temperature
  K_QUARTZ    = 1.4 W/m·K      ; thermal conductivity (conceptual)
  MASS_ROD    = 0.8 g          ; rod mass (conceptual)
  C_QUARTZ    = 0.75 J/g·°C    ; specific heat (conceptual)

  ELECTRICAL MODEL
  ----------------
  I = V / R_COIL
  P = V * I

  R_COIL(T) = R_COIL * (1 + ALPHA_T * (T_ROD - T_AMBIENT))

  THERMAL MODEL
  -------------
  dT/dt = (P - LOSS) / (MASS_ROD * C_QUARTZ)

  LOSS = K_QUARTZ * (T_ROD - T_AMBIENT)

  QUARTZ ROD BEHAVIOR
  -------------------
  • Quartz acts as a thermal buffer.
  • Temperature rises according to dT/dt.
  • Resistance increases slightly with temperature.
  • No exposed metal in this abstract model.

  LOGIC MODEL (TAMA STYLE)
  ------------------------
  STATE_ROD = {
      R: R_COIL(T),
      T: T_ROD,
      P: P,
      I: I
  }

  UPDATE_ROD():
      T_ROD += dT/dt
      R_COIL = R_COIL(T_ROD)

  SAFETY FLAGS
  ------------
  FLAG_OVERHEAT = (T_ROD > T_LIMIT)
  FLAG_OVERCURRENT = (I > I_LIMIT)
  FLAG_FAULT = FLAG_OVERHEAT OR FLAG_OVERCURRENT

